wikipedia_extract: Ume (梅; "Japanese apricot") was one of 18 Matsu-class escort destroyers
  built for the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) near the end of World War II. Completed
  in mid-1944, the ship spent her short career escorting troop and supply convoys.
  She played a minor role in the Battle of Ormoc Bay in early December, escorting
  a troop convoy in the Philippines, and was damaged there by American aircraft a
  week later. After repairs that lasted until January 1945, the ship led a small group
  of destroyers back to the Philippines in an attempt to evacuate aircrew, but was
  sunk by American bombers near Japanese Taiwan on the last day of the month.
